course: dictionary
lesson: 7010
title: Pardon: sorry, or forgiven
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word pardon has a few meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one. Most often it is a polite word you say when you did not hear someone. «Pardon?» means «Please say that again.»
explain: You can also say «Pardon me» after a small accident, like bumping into someone. It means sorry or excuse me. People also joke, «Pardon my French!», after they swear, pretending the rude word was from another language.
explain: In news and history, pardon is a serious word. A president, king or governor can pardon a person, which means they officially decide that the person will not be punished for their crime. «He was pardoned in 2013» means he was officially forgiven and freed from punishment.
explain: As a verb, pardon means to forgive someone or free them from punishment. Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if «pardon» still makes sense as «forgive», you have got it.
fact: Pardon means «please say that again» when used as «Pardon?».
fact: «Pardon my French!» is a joke, said after swearing.
fact: In Britain today, «Pardon?» and «Sorry?» are both polite ways to ask someone to repeat themselves.
fact: «Pardon» as an official decision means a person will not be punished for a crime.
fact: The verb forms are pardon, pardons, pardoned and pardoning.
exercise: After bumping into a friend, you say «Pardon me». What does it mean? | Well done, you won | *Sorry, excuse me | I am very angry | Go away now
exercise: Someone speaks quietly and you did not hear. You say «Pardon?» What does it mean? | Please go away | *Please say that again | I know the answer | I am very angry
exercise: «He was pardoned in 2013.» What does pardoned mean here? | Taught something new in school | Moved to another town | Given a prize for his work | *Officially forgiven, so no punishment
test: Which word means to forgive someone or free them from punishment? | Pardon | Pardoned in a race | Apology cake | *Pardon, as a verb: to forgive
test: «I beg your pardon» is used to mean what? | Please, I want more food | Goodbye, see you soon | You are very rude | *Sorry, or please repeat that
exam: Why would someone say «Pardon my French!» after swearing? | To ask for a translation | To show they are angry | To ask someone to repeat a word | *To apologise with a joke
